:: day0_npc_maids2 [nobr]
<h3>The Gossiping Maids — Different Pair</h3>

<p>Two different handmaidens this time — older, more senior. They're not whispering. They're standing at the junction near the east wing, arms full of linens, speaking in low tones that aren't quite whispers but aren't normal volume either. The tone of people who know something significant is happening and are trying to process it through the lens of clean sheets.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">MAID</span>"—Mistress Alva ordered the ritual chamber linens. The silver ones. Last used for the King's funeral preparation—"</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">MAID</span>"They're not for a funeral. They're for the Moonspire. I saw them being carried across the bridge this morning."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">MAID</span>"The Moonspire? But those linens are for—"</div>

<p>They see me. The silence is immediate but different from three days ago — not guilty, not startled. Sympathetic. These women know. Not the specifics, perhaps, but the shape of it. The palace has had three days to sense that something is coming, and the senior staff — the ones who've been here long enough to read the signs — have pieced it together.</p>

<p>The older of the two curtsies. Deep. Formal. The kind of curtsy you give a prince, yes, but also the kind you give someone you might not see again in the same form.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">MAID</span>"Your Highness. Safe travels."</div>

<p><em>Safe travels.</em> Not <em>good morning.</em> Not <em>how are you.</em> Safe travels. As if I'm going somewhere far away. Which I am — farther than any ship could carry me.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Thank you."</div>

<p>I walk on. Their silence follows me like a veil.</p>

<<set $d0_npc_maids2 to true>>
<<set $stress += 3>>

